{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nEvery **attested-source** LLM gate operation fails on the LIVE MCP server\n(`https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp`, container `compose-mcp-1`, image\n`compose-mcp:9499312eb7b05dc3d75d39c23ab74a5b4afc26b5`).\n\nObserved 2026-08-27 against the live endpoint:\n\n```\nreview_plan       {\"ticket_id\": \"ruby-griffinish-goitered\"}\n  -> Error executing tool review_plan: cannot resolve ref 'origin/main' to a commit in '.'.\nreview_plan       {\"ticket_id\": \"...\", \"ref\": \"HEAD\"}\n  -> Error executing tool review_plan: cannot resolve ref 'HEAD' to a commit in '.'.\nverify_completion {\"ticket_id\": \"...\"}\n  -> Error executing tool verify_completion: cannot resolve ref 'origin/main' to a commit in '.'.\nreview_plan       {\"ticket_id\": \"...\", \"source\": \"local\"}   -> RUNS (P1/P2/P3 emitted)\n```\n\n## Mechanism\nThe container's repo root has **no git metadata at all**. Verified in-container:\n\n```\n$ docker exec compose-mcp-1 sh -c 'pwd; ls -d /app/.git; git -C /app rev-parse origin/main'\n/app\nls: cannot access '/app/.git': No such file or directory\nfatal: not a git repository (or any of the parent directories): .git\n```\n\n`docker inspect` confirms `WorkingDir=/app`, `Cmd=[\"rebar-mcp\"]`, and the env carries\n`REBAR_TRACKER_DIR=/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets` but **no `REBAR_ROOT`** — so the repo root\nresolves to the cwd `/app`, which is a plain source copy, not a work tree. The image ships\n`/app/.deployed_ref` (`d4a0a2a44 (feat/gerrit-ci-verified-gate)`) as a text marker instead of a\nreal clone. `source=attested` pins a snapshot at `ref` against that root's object DB, so ref\nresolution fails before any LLM call.\n\nThe tracker itself is unaffected: it is an out-of-tree clone reached via `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR`,\nso all non-git tools (create/show/search/list/comment/edit/link/claim/transition) work.\n\n## Impact\n`attested` is the DEFAULT source for both gate ops, and a `local`-source verdict is never\nsigned. So **no plan-review or completion attestation can be earned through the live MCP\nserver**, and consequently no `task`/`story`/`epic` can be closed through it while\n`verify.require_plan_review_for_close` is on — the only remaining path is `--force`, which\nagents are prohibited from using. Reproduced live: probe task `ruby-griffinish-goitered`\n(`c67b-ece5-707e-460e`) is stuck `in_progress` with\n`plan-review close gate: unsigned: no certified plan-review attestation`, and the prescribed\nremedy (`review-plan`) is the very operation that cannot run.\n\n## Reproduction\n1. Call `review_plan` on any claimable ticket through the live MCP endpoint with default args.\n2. Observe `cannot resolve ref 'origin/main' to a commit in '.'`.\n3. Repeat with `source: \"local\"` and observe it runs.\n\n## Fix\n\nProvision a real repository for the gate ops to resolve against, and point the repo root at it.\n\n**Why not the obvious alternatives.** Shipping `.git` in the image (removing the\n`.dockerignore:5` exclusion) bloats every layer and pins a main that goes stale the moment the\nimage is built — the gates need a ref that tracks main, not a frozen one. Re-using the tickets\nclone at `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` is tempting since `MCP_TICKETS_URL` is the SAME repository, but it\nconflates the code root with the tracker: two different lifetimes, two different refspecs, and\na reader can no longer tell which one a failure came from.\n\n**Shape.** `provision_store` gains a sibling that clones the CODE side into\n`/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code` — `--filter=blob:none --single-branch --branch main`, so it is a\nblobless clone that fetches objects on demand rather than materializing the history — and\n`REBAR_ROOT` is set to it (compose env + `mcp_run_new`, which must stay in parity). That root\ncarries `rebar.toml`, so config resolution moves from the source copy at `/app` to a real\ncheckout, which is strictly better: the two agree today, and a real root is what the config\nseam expects.\n\n**Ordering.** Like the tickets clone this is backgrounded, so it cannot block `exec` past the\nreadiness deadline. Until it converges the gates fail exactly as they do today — no worse.\n\n**Enforcement is OUT OF SCOPE** (operator ruling, 2026-08-27). This change makes the attested\ngates work; it does NOT add a deploy-time check that refuses to promote a container whose code\nroot failed to resolve. A failed code clone therefore degrades to today's behaviour — the\ngates error — rather than blocking the deploy. That is a deliberate boundary, not an oversight:\ngating promotion on a backgrounded clone is what produced the rollback loop in\n`unfit-beneficial-whimbrel`, and re-introducing it here would trade one outage shape for\nanother.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] AC1: `review_plan` with default arguments against the deployed MCP server returns a plan-review verdict (PASS/BLOCK/INDETERMINATE) rather than a ref-resolution error.\n- [ ] AC2: `verify_completion` with default arguments likewise returns a completion verdict.\n- [ ] AC3: A PASS from AC1 persists a signed plan-review attestation, so `plan_review_status` on that ticket reports `certified`.\n- [ ] AC4: The deployed container exposes a git object DB for the repo root reachable by the gate ops (a real clone at the repo root, or an explicit `REBAR_ROOT` pointing at one), verified by `git -C <root> rev-parse origin/main` succeeding inside the container.\n\n## Definition of Done\n- [ ] DD1: AC1-AC3 demonstrated against a deployed MCP server.\n\n## Scope boundaries (operator rulings, 2026-08-27)\n\n- **Enforcement is out of scope.** No deploy-time refusal; see the Fix section.\n- **A shared op-cert is acceptable.** The server signing under the box's existing opcert\n  environment (ADR 0104 §3, Option A) is the accepted design. The separate observation that\n  the environment holds no public key, so `verify_signature` returns `foreign_key`, is tracked\n  as `dire-expectable-terrapin` and is NOT in scope here.\n\n- [ ] **LIVE VALIDATION — REQUIRED TO CLOSE.** `review_plan` (and `scan_spec`) called through the deployed endpoint returns a VERDICT rather than `cannot resolve ref ... in '.'`, and a certified attestation is persisted.\n      Evidence must be OBSERVED against the deployed server at\n      `https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp` and recorded in a ticket comment naming\n      the tool(s) called, the arguments, and the actual response. A passing local test is\n      NOT sufficient, and neither is a merged change: the container must have redeployed\n      and served the call. This exists because a fix here was previously reported complete\n      on the strength of a merge while the deployed behaviour was still broken.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787860086497732001,"uuid":"a793823e-1507-4734-990e-8fc193cf9e28"}